==Enemy==
Cyberhorn essentially works the same as One Horn, just with a lower money net drop and a little more range and movement speed. Cyberhorn's trait is also harder to counter, as there are more [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Reds]] than there are [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Aliens]].

Since his stats are already quite high, the effect of having insufficient [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] will be very noticeable with him.

==Strategy==
His lower money drop makes it riskier to go all out on him, but in most cases you should still aim to take him out as fast as possible. A stack of [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]] with support from [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocats]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cats]] will make quick work of Cyberhorn. However, you should take care to defeat this enemy before your [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] slip up and he advances. [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Solar Cat]] is a great offensive option, especially in [[True Form]]; and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] can effectively stall Cyberhorn, as long as his buff is not too high. And, of course, [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] with anti-Alien abilities such as the [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Heroes]] and [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] work fantastic against him.

